Description: Study of logical and physical aspects of database management systems. Entity-
Relationship (ER) and relational models for databases are presented. Relational algebra operations,
SQL queries, physical database design methods, and operating principles of database systems are
discussed.



Topics:
 DBMS concepts and architecture (Chap 1, 2)
 Entity-Relationship (ER) model (Chap 3)
 Relational data model (Chap 5)
 ER to Relational mapping (Sec. 9.1)
 Relational algebra (Chap 8)
 SQL − a relational database language (Chap 6, 7)
 File organizations and hashing (Chap 16)
